# Logging & Observability

Logs exist to understand **production behavior**, not just to debug locally.

## Plan Before Logging

Before adding or changing logs:

1. Identify workflows
2. Identify state transitions
3. Identify external dependencies
4. Identify metrics that dashboards should show

Only then implement logging changes.

---

## Required Coverage

### External Services

- Authentication success/failure
- Token refresh
- API failures, retries, latency

### Core Workflows

- Sync triggers
- Sheets processed per run
- Records read/updated
- Emails sent
- Follow-up execution counts

### System Health

- Startup configuration summary
- Enabled features
- Background job lifecycle
- Degraded modes

---

## Log Levels (Strict)

| Level | Purpose |
| ---- | ---- |
| INFO | High-level behavior, metrics |
| WARN | Recoverable issues |
| ERROR | Failed operations |
| DEBUG | Detailed internals |

Never log secrets, tokens, or PII.

Prefer structured, aggregatable logs.
